				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-919474/the-choir-below#post-2067779</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 12 Jul 2014 04:19:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aelanna</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>334454</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>(edit: I think the overflow:auto should take care of the others? don't want to screw too much with it, so only putting it after the footnoteblock)</p> </blockquote> <p>No. Floating elements are removed from the document flow entirely, and as such overflow doesn't detect, affect, or otherwise care about floating elements. The only way to ensure that a floating element fits within a container is to use a clearing line.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
